#>plan_state_block_projections_wip
#:operation #!cache
#:fixity #!tending
#:layer #!pragmatics

@plan: ~"./PLAN.md"
@index: ~"./index.spw"
@plans_root: ~"../../../.agents/plans/index.spw"
@wip_notebook: ~"../../../.spw/conventions/wip-notebook.spw"

operation = "cache"
fixity = "tending"

^"selection_probes"{
 probes = #[ `rg 'state-block-projections' public/js/site.js`, `Hypotheses: small code-like state blocks will make component state easier to read and will deepen the interaction grammar when tokens mutate real underlying state`, `test -f public/js/site.js`, ][reg=set]
 rule = "Run probes before trusting cached plan_context."
}[reg=facet]

^"plan_context"{
 goal = `The site should expose more of its live state through its own notation instead of explaining interaction only in prose. Small code-like state blocks should summarize what a component can currently do, and on selected surfaces they should let the visitor cycle operator, brace, mode, or value state directly from the block itself. The taste note is clarity + expressiveness: the blocks should feel like useful diagnostic surfaces, not novelty stickers, and they should only mutate state that the underlying component already owns.`
 owner = `state-block-projections`
 operation = "prime"
 bucket = "active_backlog"
 validation = #[ `Hypotheses: small code-like state blocks will make component state easier to read and will deepen the interaction grammar when tokens mutate real underlying state`, `Negative controls: existing mode-switch buttons, image helper chips, and settings form interactions must continue working normally`, `Demo sequence: open home hero and swap mode/operator/brace from the state block; open Pretext and cycle lens state from the block; open settings and cycle a small set of appearance/runtime values from the block; mark an image visited and confirm the image state block updates`, ][reg=set]
 hot_files = #[ `public/js/site.js`, `.agents/plans/state-block-projections/state-block-projections.spw`, ][reg=set]
}[reg=facet]
^["roots"]{
 @plan: ~"PLAN.md"
 @pattern: ~"../../../.spw/_workbench/.spw/patterns/literate-ui.spw"
 @references: ~"../interaction-grammar/PLAN.md"
 @references: ~"../archive/brace-literacy-guides/PLAN.md"
 @artifact: ~"state-block-projections.spw"
}

^["intent"]{
 ~#goal: "Expose real component state through small interactive Spw code blocks that can mutate operator, brace, mode, or settings values where those mutations are already meaningful."
 ~#taste: "clarity + expressiveness"
}

^["development"]{
 lane: #execution_truth
 ladder: #service
 develops: [#interaction_grammar, #runtime_legibility, #state_projection]
 review_surfaces: [@plan, @pattern]
 snippet_routes: [#example, #query, #snippet]
}

^["concept_index"]{
 primary: [#state_blocks, #operator_swap, #brace_swap]
 surfaces: [#home, #pretext, #settings, #images]
 tensions: [#noise, #truth, #containment]
 transfers: [#language, #component, #page, #service]
}

^["recursive_improvement"]{
 loop: [
  "? reread active runtime files before widening scope",
  "< ship one truthful state surface before adding more",
  "$ record where notation clarified interaction vs where it only decorated it",
  "^ fold working patterns back into plan and artifact",
  "% keep mutation scoped to explicitly opt-in components",
 ]
 gates: [#preview_truth, #claim_discipline, #containment]
}

^["parallel_work"]{
 critical_path: [#site_runtime]
 parallelizable: [#markup_opt_ins, #css_surface]
 shared_hot_files: ["public/js/site.js?v=0.0.2", "public/css/spw-components.css", "public/js/spw-image-metaphysics.js"]
 merge_risks: [#runtime_wiring, #overlay_containment]
 handoff_artifacts: [@plan, @artifact]
}

^["supporting_documents"]{
 must_ship: [@plan, @artifact]
 helpful: [@pattern]
 carries: [#examples, #review_notes, #source_map]
}

^["interaction_depth"]{
 subjects: [#navigation, #feedback, #preview, #legibility, #trust]
 questions: [#what_is_primary, #what_is_reversible, #what_is_visible]
 qualities: [#clarity, #rhythm, #containment]
}

^["validation"]{
 hypotheses: ["state blocks improve legibility when they mutate real state", "home/pretext/settings/images are enough to prove the pattern without flooding the site"]
 negative_controls: ["existing controls remain usable", "image helper behavior remains intact", "settings changes still persist through site-settings.js"]
 demo_path: ["/#home-frame", "/topics/software/pretext/#pretext-field-lab", "/settings/#runtime-preferences"]
}

^["stream"]{
 >>[2026-04-11 09:03] observe — Gemini left partial state/projection scaffolding in site.js, spw-components.css, spw-grammar.css, and spw-image-metaphysics.js
 >>[2026-04-11 09:06] decide — narrow the feature to truthful state blocks on home, pretext, settings, and image surfaces instead of site-wide overlays
 >>[2026-04-11 09:08] taste — the block must read like a useful code surface first; interactivity is secondary
 >>[2026-04-11 09:31] implement — repaired the broken image hold timer, added image refresh hooks, and opted home/pretext/settings into explicit state inspection
 >>[2026-04-11 09:34] align — copy now frames the block as an epistemic boundary handle: stance, containment, and persisted mode/setting changes remain visible and reversible
 >>[2026-04-11 09:53] refine — state blocks now expose a small explicit loop state (preview, activated, resolved) so actions read as deliberate processes rather than anonymous clicks
 >>[2026-04-11 09:57] integrate — image helper, hold-to-visit, mode switches, and settings changes now resolve through shared refresh / change paths instead of isolated flashes
 >>[2026-10-12 10:59] verify — the cache's "implementing" from April no longer holds. The inspector runtime (public/js/interface/state-inspector.js) and the lens-seat bench at /design/components/#lens-seats (dc7c35a7) are built, and the next slice, moving the chosen seat out of routes/surfaces/design.css into handles/operators/state-semantics.css, waits on the creator picking A, B or C in a browser. The same review settles the faint mode-switch chips and the lens reward; runtime/memory/component-collection.js still has no spw:variant-selected listener.
 >>[2026-10-25 17:45] verify — Read against the tree for the UI review sitting: state-semantics.css already holds the silent and quiet lens-chrome values (:135-136, :229-279), and only seat is bench-only (design.css:1686), so Status now moves only seat and names the look, live on a phone and a desktop at /design/components/#lens-seats, with Row 1 judged in the same look. Fixed the image-metaphysics path (public/js/media/), marked brace-literacy-guides archived, and gave Row 2, the menu toggle, to chrome-navigation-wonder.
 >>[2026-10-25 19:26] implement — At the creator's ask, the lens concept and its UX, without the seat choice: the seat a page opens on reweights nothing (html[data-spw-active-lens-source] reads initial until a reader picks or a link names a seat); Home's receding cards keep AA contrast at 0.72 (their text measured 2.5:1 at the old 0.42, 6.2:1 now); each Home seat's panel says what it keeps bright below, linked; the seats point at their panels (aria-controls) and the panels announce politely. A reader's pick buzzes and is remembered in the address as ?spw-lens=, because bare ?lens= is the legible-channel setting and the settings sync was dropping every seat written there; the opening and query writes stay silent. Seat A, B or C is still the creator's look.
 >>[2026-10-25 20:05] implement — The lens's reach and contour: ten Home frames and the four cards say which seats they serve; a chosen seat outlines its frames in its operator color and the lens feedback counts the places that answer. A pick no longer focuses its frame: it had dimmed every other frame to 0.62 and, through pointer-events: none, left 83 of 93 controls in them untappable on a phone. Dimmed frames now never block input and hold AA at 0.88 with grayscale.
 >>[2026-10-25 20:40] implement — The lens reads the page's Spw. lens-reach.js reads each frame two ways and keeps them apart: declared by the page (data-spw-lens-pass) and parsed from the frame's handles through the operator table, as a lift of the seat's operator over its page share. A frame carries declared, parsed or both on data-spw-lens-reach, outlined solid, dashed or double in the seat's color, and the feedback names the readings apart. On Home they meet on one frame for Build and one for Play; Study and Studio's marks are rare in Home's handles, so their parsed reach is two frames and one. Expression kin (the build-time parse) was measured and left out: Home's frame expressions share no words with the seats' own.
}

